text:
alex: Quick question — can someone confirm expected semantics for POST /v1/serve/select when callers send both model_id and routing hints? I hit an edge where old SDKs only sent model_id and newer clients send route hints too. Example payload I tried: ```{
  "model_id": "redwood-7b",
  "routing": {
    "region": "eu-west-1",
    "tier": "standard",
    "hint": "low-latency"
  }
}```
maria: Short answer: model_id should be authoritative (treated as a pin). routing hints are advisory and used for selection only when model_id is a family/alias or absent. We need to document fallback behavior though.
tariq: That aligns with current runtime: if model_id resolves to a concrete served model we prefer it; if model_id resolves to a family alias or is missing we run the routing policy using hints/region/tier to pick a variant. We also add a served_model.reason field with value like "pinned" or "route_match" for observability.
alex: Nice. What about backward compatibility — older SDKs that omit routing should still get the same model when they explicitly set model_id, right? Concern is we might start routing them into different region if we prioritize tier/region hints globally.
maria: Correct — preserve existing behavior for explicit model_id. Important nuance: if model_id is an alias (e.g., "redwood-7b-latest") and we roll a new variant, routing hints may affect which variant is chosen across regions. So we should avoid changing default alias resolution semantics.
tariq: Proposal: rule set = [1) if model_id is concrete (served model id) -> serve that model; 2) else if model_id is alias or absent -> use routing.hint/region/tier with policy to pick best match; 3) always include served_model.{id,variant,reason} in response]. Also add a compatibility flag in response: served_model.backcompat = "explicit_pin"|"routed_alias".
sam-bot: deploy-bot: CI check: api-spec linter flagged missing example for select endpoint.
alex: OK can someone file a tiny spec PR adding the explicit precedence rules + example request/response and a paragraph about alias semantics? I can review.
maria: I'll take it. I'll add example responses: ```{
  "served_model": {
    "id": "redwood-7b-v1",
    "variant": "int8-optimized",
    "reason": "pinned",
    "backcompat": "explicit_pin"
  }
}``` and a second example for routed alias. Will include a note for SDKs: if you want region/tier routing override, pass routing.force_region = true (new opt-in flag) — default false to avoid surprising changes.
alex: Perfect. ETA?
maria: PR opened: https://git.internal/redwood/api-spec/pull/412 — description and examples included. Requesting review from @alex and @tariq. :thumbsup:
